================================================================================
  ORIGINAL LICENSE NOTE FROM THE lamejs PACKAGE
================================================================================

  Can I use LAME in my commercial program?

  Yes, you can, under the restrictions of the LGPL. The easiest way to do
  this is to:

    1. Link to LAME as a separate library (lame.min.js / lame.all.js /
       lamejs.iife.js, etc.).

    2. Fully acknowledge that you are using LAME, and give a link to the
       lame.sourceforge.net web site.

    3. If you make modifications to LAME, you *must* release those
       modifications back to the LAME project, under the LGPL.

